From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: swear01 <stanley.yellow1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:15:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/95] fix(claude): keep mid-turn steers recoverable until
 Claude takes them

Addresses the open HAPI Bot findings on upstream PR #2008 (head 4c22ab47):

- Treat command_lifecycle support as unknown until Claude reports one or
  a turn ends without any, so steers sent during startup stay tracked.
- Stop the Claude process before restoring unstarted steers on an early
  tool-abort return, so the old process cannot run them a second time.
- Discard the prompt echo marker only when cancellation removes the row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
